From: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: pci: enable AQL

rtw89 has no airtime queue limits: mac80211 hands over frames as long as
the DMA rings have room (256 descriptors per AC, each for a frame or an
A-MSDU), shared by all stations. Under load the queue builds up in the
hardware, where the fq_codel of mac80211 can neither see nor manage it.

Enable AQL for PCI devices. mac80211 estimates the airtime of each frame
from the last TX rate of the station, which rtw89 doesn't report yet:
pass the rate of each firmware RA report to mac80211 with a rate-only
ieee80211_tx_status_ext(). A station over its limit is held back until
TX completions return its airtime; the TX queue work now runs on TX
completion, so its frames go out then. Every TX frame ends in
ieee80211_tx_status_ni() or ieee80211_free_txskb(), which return the
airtime of the frame.

Signed-off-by: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
---
diff --git drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/pci.c drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/pci.c
index bdfdc69..3da69e5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/pci.c
@@ -5104,6 +5104,9 @@ int rtw89_pci_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 		rtwdev->hw->max_tx_fragments = RTW89_TXADDR_INFO_NR_V1;
 	}
 
+	/* TX completions kick the TX queues (rtw89_pci_poll_rpq_dma()) */
+	wiphy_ext_feature_set(rtwdev->hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL);
+
 	ret = rtw89_core_register(rtwdev);
 	if (ret) {
 		rtw89_err(rtwdev, "failed to register core\n");
diff --git drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/phy.c drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/phy.c
index 759be4d..05e0701 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/phy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/phy.c
@@ -3237,6 +3237,12 @@ static void __rtw89_phy_c2h_ra_rpt_iter(struct rtw89_sta_link *rtwsta_link,
 	struct rtw89_ra_report *ra_report = &rtwsta_link->ra_report;
 	const struct rtw89_chip_info *chip = rtwdev->chip;
 	bool format_v1 = chip->chip_gen == RTW89_CHIP_BE;
+	struct ieee80211_rate_status rate_status = {};
+	struct ieee80211_tx_status tx_status = {
+		.sta = rtwsta_link_to_sta(rtwsta_link),
+		.rates = &rate_status,
+		.n_rates = 1,
+	};
 	u8 mode, rate, bw, giltf, mac_id;
 	u16 legacy_bitrate, amsdu_len;
 	u8 retry_ratio = 0;
@@ -3339,6 +3345,10 @@ static void __rtw89_phy_c2h_ra_rpt_iter(struct rtw89_sta_link *rtwsta_link,
 	ra_report->retry_ratio = retry_ratio;
 	ra_report->might_fallback_legacy = mcs <= 2;
 
+	/* the expected airtime of AQL is based on the last TX rate */
+	rate_status.rate_idx = ra_report->txrate;
+	ieee80211_tx_status_ext(rtwdev->hw, &tx_status);
+
 	amsdu_len = get_max_amsdu_len(rtwdev, ra_report);
 	if (link_sta->agg.max_rc_amsdu_len != amsdu_len) {
 		link_sta->agg.max_rc_amsdu_len = amsdu_len;
